# Spartan engine workflow

Work in the live engine through the `spartan_engine` MCP server (`user-spartan_engine` namespace). Never edit `.world` files blind, and never write your own bridge clients, TCP scripts or camera/screenshot helpers; the MCP already exposes them. If the MCP cannot do something, tell the user instead of working around it.

## Session start
1. `GetDynamicTools` on `user-spartan_engine`. If it is missing or errored, stop and tell the user (config lives in `~/.cursor/mcp.json`, server `tools/mcp/spartan_engine/server.mjs`, port set by `--port=`).
2. `agent_memory_read`, then `context_snapshot`.
3. If the bridge does not answer, launch the engine from `binaries/`: `spartan_vulkan_development.exe --mcp-control --mcp-port=<port from mcp.json> --no-steam`, then `world_load` with an absolute path (e.g. `C:/Users/panos/Desktop/spartan_engine/worlds/plan.world`) and poll `context_snapshot` until `loading` is false.
4. Never close or kill a Spartan instance you did not start; another agent may be using it.

## Iterate by looking
- Before changing anything, frame the area with `camera_set_view` (position + target, world space) and capture `screenshot_take` with `wait_ms`. Keep a fixed set of named viewpoints so before/after shots are comparable.
- After every meaningful change, re-shoot the same viewpoints, look at the images, critique scale, composition, lighting and materials, and iterate. Show the key screenshots to the user.
- Resolve entities with `entity_resolve` and read world transforms from it; parent-local coordinates must be converted with the parent's position and yaw.
- Prefer native tools: `mesh_generate` / `mesh_generate_batch` / `compound_create` for geometry, `material_textured_create` / `texture_generate` for surfaces, `entity_create_light` for every light, batch transform tools for many entities. Use `search_capabilities` before guessing tool names. Lua only for small, known-binding scripts.
- Mutations need edit mode (`engine_set_mode`); `camera_set_view` also works in paused play mode.
- Save with `world_save` only when the user wants the change persisted; check `git status worlds/` first so another agent's edits are not overwritten.

## Authored hero areas (Blender pipelines)
Some locations are generated offline and installed into the world, e.g. the player garage in `binaries/project/home_garage` (see its `README.md`):
`sources/upgrade_home_garage.mjs` (native furniture via MCP) -> Blender `--background --python sources/build_home_garage.py` -> `sources/import_home_garage.mjs` -> `sources/install_home_garage.py`.
Edit the source scripts, not the baked `.mesh` files or the world XML, then rebuild, reload the world in the engine and verify with screenshots. The `user-blender` MCP can be used to inspect `sources/*.blend` files visually.

## Finish
- Append durable lessons to `tools/mcp/spartan_engine/AGENT_MEMORY.md` with `agent_memory_append`.
- Report what changed with before/after screenshots and anything the MCP could not do.
